DreamTileView:TileAlignment {
    at    Source/DreamGUIControls/Public/Controls/DreamTileView.h#DreamTileView:TileAlignment
    src   "How a line's tiles are distributed across the width -- UMG's TileAlignment.\n\nLeftAligned, not UMG's EvenlyDistributed: it is what every tile view in this library has drawn,\nand a grid that silently re-spaced itself on upgrade would be a layout change nobody asked for."
    text  "一行图块在其宽度上如何分布——即对齐，UMG的TileAlignment。\n\n默认为LeftAligned，而非UMG的EvenlyDistributed：这是本库中每个图块视图一直绘制出的样子，\n而一个在升级时悄悄改变间距的网格，是没人要求过的布局变化。"
    state machine
}

EDreamTileAlignment {
    at    Source/DreamGUIControls/Public/Controls/DreamTileView.h#EDreamTileAlignment
    src   "How a line's tiles are distributed across the width it has -- UMG's EListItemAlignment, with its\nseven answers and its names.\n\nThe distinction worth holding on to is WHAT each one spends the leftover space on. Three of them\nmove the line without changing it (Left/Right/Center), two put the slack into the gaps or the\ncells and leave the tile alone (EvenlyDistributed, EvenlyWide), and two grow the tile itself\n(EvenlySize, Fill) -- differing only in whether a short last line grows with the rest."
    text  "一行图块在其拥有的宽度上如何分布——即对齐，UMG的EListItemAlignment及其\n七种取值和名称。\n\n值得把握的区别在于每一种把剩余空间花在哪里。其中三种\n只移动整行而不改变它（Left/Right/Center），两种把余量放进间隙或\n单元格而保持图块不变（EvenlyDistributed、EvenlyWide），还有两种会放大图块\n本身（EvenlySize、Fill）——区别仅在于较短的末行是否随其余行一起放大。"
    state machine
}

